\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Corrective-nudge behavior split by reference type. \emph  {GT-anchored}: the locate call was ground-truth-grounded (annotated tooth; pathology cohorts) and the reference box is the expert box. \emph  {Detector-anchored}: exploratory calls (dominated by healthy-scan full-arch surveys), where the reference is the detector's own box. During rapid surveys the teacher corrects far less often per box, a difference in behavior that pooled rates would hide.}}{24}{table.caption.45}\protected@file@percent }
